{"shortDescription":"Chicago soybean futures rose for a third session on Wednesday, supported by Chinese demand and doubts over U.S. supply levels, analysts said.Corn and wheat edged lower, curbed by weaker crude oil and lingering hopes of diplomatic progress to resolve war disruption to Black Sea grain trade.The most…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Chicago soybean futures rose for a third session on Wednesday, supported by Chinese demand and doubts over U.S. supply levels, analysts said."]},{"type":"p","children":["Corn and wheat edged lower, curbed by weaker crude oil and lingering hopes of diplomatic progress to resolve war disruption to Black Sea grain trade."]},{"type":"p","children":["The most-active soybean contract ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"CBOT:ZS1!","text":"CBOT:ZS1!"}}," on the Chicago Board of Trade ended the overnight session up 0.6% at $13.26-3/4 a bushel."]},{"type":"p","children":["Soybean prices remained supported by a rise in Chinese demand for U.S. supplies ahead of Chinese President Xi Jinping's expected visit to Washington later this month."]},{"type":"p","children":["The market was also digesting a monthly industry report showing that August soybean crushing in the U.S. was lower than expected, stirring concerns about availability of soymeal and soyoil."]},{"type":"p","children":["Concerns over harvest delays also lent support to soybean and corn prices. Harvesting was under way across the U.S. Midwest, but showers this week are expected to hamper field work."]},{"type":"p","children":["In Brazil, crop agency Conab forecast the country's 2026/27 soybean production at 181.64 million metric tons, up 0.7% from the previous year but below the U.S. Department of Agriculture's current forecast of 186 million metric tons."]},{"type":"p","children":["CBOT wheat ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"CBOT:ZW1!","text":"CBOT:ZW1!"}}," was down 0.2% at $7.27 a bushel and corn ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"CBOT:ZC1!","text":"CBOT:ZC1!"}}," inched down 0.1% to $5.35-1/4 a bushel."]},{"type":"p","children":["Wheat has recovered from a 2-1/2-week low on Monday when U.S. President Donald Trump announced a commitment by Russia and Ukraine to halt strikes on energy sites."]},{"type":"p","children":["But further attacks on infrastructure have tempered hopes of de-escalation that could in turn ease disruption to Black Sea shipments."]},{"type":"p","children":["Algeria's state grains agency OAIC bought about 500,000 metric tons of wheat in a tender that closed on Tuesday, while Pakistan has received offers in a tender seeking 750,000 tons, traders said."]},{"type":"p","children":["The corn market was digesting Conab's forecast of a record Brazilian crop in 2026/27."]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Prices at 1257 GMT"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Last"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Change"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Pct Move"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["CBOT wheat ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"CBOT:ZW1!","text":"CBOT:ZW1!"}}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["727.00"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["-1.50"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["-0.21"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["CBOT corn ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"CBOT:ZC1!","text":"CBOT:ZC1!"}}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","chi